      ],
      "source": "https://carterethistory.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town is framed by Pettiford Creek to the north, the Croatan National Forest to the east, and Cedar Point to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Carteret%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bogue Sound lies to the south, with Emerald Isle across the water, linked to Cape Carteret by the Bogue Sound Bridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Carteret%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cape Carteret blends small‑town charm with easy access to the Crystal Coast’s natural beauty.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.crystalcoastnc.org/towns/cape-carteret/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Families can enjoy mini‑golf, go‑karts, bumper boats, and a 4,000‑square‑foot arcade right in town.",
